  "notes": "Logo: header logo seal-all-round-logo.png (the 2x file; seal-all-round-logo-1.png in 2025/07 is the 1x copy). The white SOEL logo is a separate programme mark and was not used. Most trip photos are served as WordPress crops (-1550x700, -1280x700 and similar); each was swapped for the full-size original where that loads, and repeats of the same file were merged. The 700x500 cards on each page are the related tours strip and were left out. Screenshot PNGs on some pages are listed last so the importer can drop them; the Mindfulness, Yoga & Wildlife page has only a screenshot. Videos are all on the operator's own YouTube channel (https://www.youtube.com/@seaalldolphinswims3704), embedded on the home page and the Dolphin TV page; more Dolphin TV episodes are on the channel (stingrays, gannets, spider crabs, common dolphins, Pope's Eye, lighthouses). Not used: oahagM-jHOU and ClP2RVXJ5yU (a what-we-do film and a background loop uploaded by Viewpoint Digital Media, not the operator), the 'Reef Cam by Kina Diving' photo (credited to another business) and an image named Dolphin-AI on the environmental page. Check before use: some photo file names suggest outside sources though nothing on the pages credits them: TA_SeaAllDolphins_* (likely a Tourism Australia shoot of this operator), 20230403_640_4_DavidDonnelly (a photographer's name), and the Surf School photos named surfgroms__* (downloaded from a 'surfgroms' Instagram account). No bot checks met."
